 but that have not yet resulted in visible deterioration of our credit quality measures.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/07/25/zions-bancorporation-zion-q2-2018-earnings-confere.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2018 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2018-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Harris Simmons","x":"As I just mentioned, there's still room for improvement, some of which should be achieved as we right size our capital structure but we've also come a long way since 2015.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/07/25/zions-bancorporation-zion-q2-2018-earnings-confere.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2018 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2018-07-23","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"However, using our calculated, adjusted non-interest expense, which adjusts for items such as severance, provision for unfunded lending commitments and other similar items, non-interest expense increased $22 million to $421 million from $399 million in the year-ago period, or about 5%.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/07/25/zions-bancorporation-zion-q2-2018-earnings-confere.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2018 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2018-10-22","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Harris Simmons","x":"…to reflect stressors that can be observed in the economy generally, such as the implementation of tariffs, higher interest rates and the effect that they may have on certain borrowers, and higher oil and gas prices which may reduce profit margins for certain commercial businesses and drag on…","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/22/zions-bancorp-na-zion-q3-2018-earnings-conference.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2018 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2018-10-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Harris Simmons","x":"Before we dig into the numbers, within the theme of simplification and streamlining I'd also like to note that we completed our merger of the holding company with and into the Bank, reducing organizational complexity and eliminating duplicate of regulatory oversight.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/22/zions-bancorp-na-zion-q3-2018-earnings-conference.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2018 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2018-10-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"However, adjusted non-interest expense, which adjusts for items such as severance, provision for unfunded lending commitment and other similar items, non-interest expense was very stable at $416 million versus $414 million in the year-ago period.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2018/10/22/zions-bancorp-na-zion-q3-2018-earnings-conference.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2018 Q4","e":"zion","d":"2019-01-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Paul E. Burdiss","x":"However, adjusted non-interest expense, which adjusts for items such as severance, provision for unfunded lending commitments and other similar items, was also very stable at $418 million versus $415 million in the year-ago period.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/01/22/zions-bancorp-zion-q4-2018-earnings-conference-cal.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q1","e":"zion","d":"2019-04-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Ken Zerbe","x":"And then just my related follow-up, can you just talk a little bit about your outlook for deposit price increases now that the Fed is partially done raising rates.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q1-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q1","e":"zion","d":"2019-04-22","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"We increased our outlook for loan growth to -- somewhat to moderately increasing given the recent strengths in net loan additions.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/04/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q1-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2019-07-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"We're really a little bit backward-looking in that we have continued to see deposit price increases even as short-term rates fall.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/23/zions-bancorporation-zion-q2-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2019-07-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"analyst","s":"Ken Usdin","x":"You mentioned you're still seeing the price increases and the mix.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/23/zions-bancorporation-zion-q2-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2019-07-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"Looking ahead on noninterest expense, we expect to uphold our focus on expense controls and streamlining bank operations while investing in technology and people to enable controlled -- continued business growth.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/23/zions-bancorporation-zion-q2-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2019-07-22","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"We have reduced our outlook for net interest income to stable to slightly decreasing, but I will caution you that net interest income is becoming increasingly difficult to predict in the current rate environment.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/07/23/zions-bancorporation-zion-q2-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2019-10-21","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Michael Morris","x":"Tariffs, trade war talk is adversely impacted, mostly hay, beef and grain; potatoes, a little bit; sugar beets, a little bit.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q3-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2019-10-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Harris Simmons","x":"…digital experiences for our customers with the goal of being quite competitive with the best providers of financial service products banks and nonbanks alike while remaining focused on continuous improvement and streamlining our processes, thereby keeping noninterest expense under control.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q3-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2019-10-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Harris Simmons","x":"This acceleration will result in a temporary increase in noninterest expense in the fourth quarter as severance and other similar efficiency initiative-related charges are recognized.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q3-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2019-10-21","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"In September, we reduced our outlook for net interest income to slightly decreasing from stable to slightly decreasing as the outlook for interest rates has become more negative than it was in July.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q3-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2019-10-21","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"What we were trying to say was that if you look back over the last 12 months, we had sort of a moderately increasing outlook, but what we achieved was actually better than that.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2019/10/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q3-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q4","e":"zion","d":"2020-01-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Harris Simmons","x":"Also shown is the adjusted pre-provision net revenue, which as noted, already excludes the impact of $37 million of noninterest expense related to severance and restructuring charges.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q4-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2019 Q4","e":"zion","d":"2020-01-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Harris Simmons","x":"…enhancing digital experiences for our customers with a goal of being quite competitive for the best providers, financial services products, banks and nonbanks alike, while remaining focused on continuous improvement in streamlining our processes, thereby keeping noninterest expense under control.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/01/22/zions-bancorporation-zion-q4-2019-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2020 Q1","e":"zion","d":"2020-04-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"As shown on Slide 18, the decline in noninterest expense reflects our ongoing efforts to reduce expenses and streamline operations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/21/zions-bancorporation-zion-q1-2020-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2020 Q1","e":"zion","d":"2020-04-20","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul Burdiss","x":"Ken, we specifically withdrew guidance because the environment is making sort of the trend lines in all of these key categories so difficult to predict.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/04/21/zions-bancorporation-zion-q1-2020-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2020 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2020-07-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Paul E. Burdiss","x":"As shown on Slide 18, the decline in non-interest expense reflects our ongoing efforts to reduce expenses and streamline operations.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2020/07/20/zions-bancorporation-zion-q2-2020-earnings-call-tr.aspx"},{"c":"ZION 2020 Q4","e":"zion","d":"2021-01-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Paul E. Burdiss","x":"Total compensation and benefits for the full year excluding severance was $28 million less than in 2019 or 2.5% lower.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/20/zions-bancorporation-zion-q4-2020-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"ZION 2020 Q4","e":"zion","d":"2021-01-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Paul E. Burdiss","x":"Helping to drive these savings are continued efforts to streamline and simplify our operations where possible, which has been enabled in part by our investments in technology.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/01/20/zions-bancorporation-zion-q4-2020-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"ZION 2021 Q1","e":"zion","d":"2021-04-19","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul E. Burdiss","x":"On balance, we are reasonably comfortable reiterating our slightly increasing outlook, which can be interpreted as non-PPP loan growth in the low-single digits.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/04/20/zions-bancorporation-zion-q1-2021-earnings-call-tr/"},{"c":"ZION 2021 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2021-07-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Harris H. Simmons","x":"We continue to streamline the organization allowing operational expense to remain relatively flat.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/19/zions-bancorp-na-zion-q2-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"ZION 2021 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2021-07-19","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul E. Burdiss","x":"And as such, we are modestly increasing our outlook to slightly -- to moderately increasing from slightly increasing.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/19/zions-bancorp-na-zion-q2-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"ZION 2021 Q2","e":"zion","d":"2021-07-19","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul E. Burdiss","x":"We reiterate our outlook for customer-related fees at moderately increasing.","url":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2021/07/19/zions-bancorp-na-zion-q2-2021-earnings-call-transc/"},{"c":"ZION 2021 Q3","e":"zion","d":"2021-10-18","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Paul E. Burdiss","x":"We are more optimistic about loan growth now than we were in July, and as such, we are increasing our outlook to moderately increasing from slightly to moderately increasing led by core C&I including our promotional